r hand structure or wasting your Black Joker.\n\nReason: I must prevent the Landlord from winning a trick with a low card like a 6. Playing ♠7 is the most efficient move as it is my lowest valid single that beats the 6. It preserves my strong Triplet of 8s, which I intend to use later to carry my loose ♥5 (playing 888+5). Passing risks the Landlord gaining the lead cheaply, and breaking the triplet or using the Joker now would be suboptimal.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♠7"]}'}
